# Line endings: normalized to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Windows tooling rewrites these files with CRLF, which showed 30 files as
# modified when nothing had changed — including data/raw/ and data/conformed/,
# which ARE the data freeze. Line-ending churn on the freeze is not cosmetic:
# it makes "the frozen snapshot is untouched" impossible to assert by hash, and
# would cause the freeze-integrity check in the Q2 filed build to fail on every
# run for a reason that has nothing to do with the data.
#
# Every blob in HEAD is already LF, so this is a policy declaration and not a
# rewrite: git normalizes on the way into the index and the phantom diffs stop
# appearing. No renormalization commit is needed.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never examined for line endings, never normalized.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
